  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Photographed at Gutenberg Museum, the Library of Congress, and the city of Mainz.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">An entry in the competition, "Love Letter to Gutenberg," organized by the University of Applied Studies Mainz, Department of Gestaltung, September 1999.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"...a collaboration between an American and a German student. Both travel to visit Gutenberg Bibles-one in Washington D.C., one in Mainz.... with two titles and two colophons, there is no beginning or end, no front or back to the book. Letterpress and offset printed on sturdy Japanese paper." -- Vamp and Tramp website, 4/28/2012.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition limited to 500 copies.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Single leaf is folded, accordion-style and housed in portfolio.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Printed on both sides.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Condition: no library markings, in protective enclosure.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="546" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Colophon in English and German.</subfield>
  </datafield>
